# Iconia

Iconia is a Java-based application designed to manage team registrations and communications for a tournament or event. It uses modular domain-driven design, and includes support for Twilio to send messages (SMS or WhatsApp).

---

## 📁 Project Structure

src/
└── main/
└── java/
└── org.iconia/
├── domain/
│ ├── chatManager/ # Handles user message processing and flow control
│ ├── hostManager/ # Tournament and Twilio integration logic
├── model/ # Data models and feedback wrappers
├── persistence/ # Database access logic
├── view/ # Input/output handlers and the main entry point

---

## 📦 Features

- Team creation and joining flow
- Command parsing and feedback
- Twilio integration for message delivery
- Modular design with separation of concerns

---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Wandilekubheka/sonia_agent.git
cd iconia
2. Configure .env
You must create a .env file at the project root for Twilio credentials:

TWILIO_ACC=your_account_sid
TWILIO_KEY=your_auth_token
☝️ These credentials are required for sending messages through Twilio. Get them from Twilio Console.

3. Build and Run
Use your preferred Java IDE or CLI tool (like Maven or Gradle) to build and run the project.

📞 Twilio Integration
The TwilioHelper class under domain.hostManager manages all communication via Twilio.

To send a message:
TwilioHelper.sendMessage(to, body,theMessage);

